module Main
import Std.Base

-- Typeclass / instance-dictionary baseline (Suite B, Task 9). A user class with
-- a single method elaborates to a dictionary record constructor; the instance
-- desugars to a dict CAF `dict$Describe$Shape = Describe$Dict(<method-closure>)`.
-- That CAF is an IMMORTAL GLOBAL: `runModuleRC` forces it once at load time and
-- its allocated record lives for the module's lifetime, so it counts toward the
-- baseline (baseline == 1), NOT toward a leak. `main` resolves `size` through the
-- dict (a boxed method closure applied at the call head), so the program runs on
-- the RC store as a first-order, no-handler program whose only persistent heap
-- cell is the dictionary. The heap-empty oracle therefore asserts the BASELINE
-- invariant: stLive == baseline (== 1) and allocs - frees == baseline, i.e.
-- main's dynamic Circle shell is fully reclaimed on top of the immortal dict.
class Describe a where
  size : a -> U64

data Shape = Circle U64 | Square U64

instance Describe Shape where
  size s = case s of
    Circle r -> r
    Square w -> w

main = size (Circle 7)
